# Input
```cjs
for (var i = 0; i < 10; i--) {}
```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.jsonc:1:5 lint/correctness/useValidForDirection ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The update clause in this loop moves the variable in the wrong direction.
  
  > 1 │ for (var i = 0; i < 10; i--) {}
      │     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  
  i The variable moves away from the value that ends the loop, so the loop condition may never become false. This can cause an infinite loop.
  
  i Change the update clause so that it moves the variable toward the loop condition, or change the condition.
  

```

